  'download.macos.gatekeeper.step1.title': 'macOS refuses to open the app',
  'download.macos.gatekeeper.step1.desc': 'Current DMGs are signed and notarized, so this should not happen. With an older download or a copy you built yourself, macOS may say "Apple cannot check it for malicious software."',
  'download.macos.gatekeeper.step2.title': 'Open Privacy & Security settings',
  'download.macos.gatekeeper.step2.desc': 'Go to Apple menu → System Settings → Privacy & Security. Scroll down to the Security section.',
  'download.macos.gatekeeper.step3.title': 'Click "Open Anyway"',
  'download.macos.gatekeeper.step3.desc': 'You will see a message about WhisPaste. Click "Open Anyway". This button is available for about one hour after the first launch attempt.',
  'download.macos.gatekeeper.step4.title': 'Confirm and enter your password',
  'download.macos.gatekeeper.step4.desc': 'Click "Open Anyway" again in the confirmation dialog, then enter your Mac login password when prompted.',
  'download.macos.gatekeeper.why.title': 'Why can this happen?',
  'download.macos.gatekeeper.why.desc': 'Releases are signed and notarized by Apple in the GitHub Actions build. Older downloads and self-built copies are not, and macOS shows this warning for any app it cannot verify. It does not mean the app is unsafe: the full source code is public.',
  'download.linux.title': 'Linux',
  'download.linux.desc': 'Direct download, no terminal required: make the AppImage executable and run it.',
  'download.linux.appimage.btnHint': 'Recommended · no install step',
  'download.linux.appimage.hint': 'If it does not start, install libfuse2 (on Ubuntu 24.04: libfuse2t64) or run it with --appimage-extract-and-run. Right-click the file → Properties → Permissions → "Allow executing", then double-click to run.',
  'download.linux.deb.button': 'Or the .deb package (Debian/Ubuntu)',
  'download.linux.explainerLink': 'Which Linux file do I need? AppImage, .deb and tar.gz explained →',
  'download.linux.explainerLink.href': '/en/linux-speech-to-text/',
  'download.linux.source.title': 'Build from source instead?',
  'download.linux.source.desc': 'WhisPaste is a Flutter app. Building from source needs Flutter and the speech-engine build step from BUILD.md.',
  'download.linux.build.intro': 'WhisPaste is a Flutter app. Building it on Linux needs Flutter, plus one speech-engine build step for on-device Whisper.',
  'download.linux.build.step1.title': 'Install Flutter',
  'download.linux.build.step1.desc': 'Follow the official Flutter install guide at flutter.dev. On most distributions a snap works well: `sudo snap install flutter --classic`. Run `flutter doctor` to verify the setup.',
  'download.linux.build.step2.title': 'Clone the repository',
  'download.linux.build.step2.desc': 'Run `git clone https://github.com/whispaste/whispaste.git` in a terminal and change into the directory: `cd whispaste`.',
  'download.linux.build.step3.title': 'Build and run',
  'download.linux.build.step3.desc': 'Run `flutter run -d linux` to build and launch WhisPaste. On-device Whisper also needs the speech-engine step `scripts/build-libwhisper-linux.sh` (see BUILD.md). Parakeet and cloud work without it.',
  'download.linux.build.repo': 'View source on GitHub',
