  'highlights.hotkey.title': 'Control recording',
  'highlights.hotkey.desc': 'Choose your hotkey. Press once to start recording and again to stop. With push-to-talk, recording lasts while you hold the key; this mode is experimental on Linux. Esc discards the recording.',
  'highlights.snippets.title': 'Reuse text blocks',
  'highlights.snippets.desc': 'Save recurring text as snippets. Your configured trigger word or enabled snippet hotkey opens a picker at the cursor. Choose the text you need, or fill in a template one field at a time.',
  'highlights.smartmode.title': 'Revise text with Smart Mode',
  'highlights.smartmode.desc': 'Clean up a transcript, shorten it or translate it into one of seven languages. Smart Mode is off by default. It runs locally on macOS and Windows, experimentally on Linux, or through OpenAI with your own API key.',
  'highlights.sidepanel.title': 'Reuse copied text',
  'highlights.sidepanel.desc': 'The side panel keeps transcripts, snippets and copied text within reach. Windows and macOS include clipboard history; Linux shows the most recently copied content.',
  'highlights.history.title': 'Find earlier text',
  'highlights.history.desc': 'Transcripts for the clipboard and active app are saved in your local history. Search, edit or export them as TXT, Markdown, JSON, CSV or DOCX. Quick notes stay in the notes area.',
  'highlights.privacy.title': 'Choose where processing happens',
  'highlights.privacy.desc': 'Speech recognition runs locally by default. Audio is discarded after transcription unless you enable audio retention. Usage statistics and crash reports are on by default and can be turned off separately. The privacy section explains the data paths.',
  'highlights.hardware.title': 'Work without a graphics card',
  'highlights.hardware.desc': 'WhisPaste uses supported graphics hardware through Metal or Vulkan and can also run on the CPU. At least 8 GB of RAM is required. An optional CUDA pack is available in the GitHub builds for Windows and Linux with compatible NVIDIA cards.',
  'highlights.notes.title': 'Build up a note',
  'highlights.notes.desc': 'The optional quick-note hotkey appends what you say to your designated quick note. WhisPaste then brings its window forward to show the result. No history entry is created.',
  'highlights.vocabulary.title': 'Add your own terms',
  'highlights.vocabulary.desc': 'Add names and specialist terms to your vocabulary. Use replacements to correct recurring spellings or replace a phrase you define with your own text.',
  'highlights.remote.title': 'Connect your own tools',
  'highlights.remote.desc': 'whispaste --toggle starts or stops a recording; --cancel discards it. You can also use these commands for a desktop hotkey on Wayland. whispaste --transcribe-file <wav> outputs the text of a WAV file. The optional local API is off by default and protected by a token.',
  'highlights.access.title': 'Start recording with a click',
  'highlights.access.desc': 'You can also start recordings from the tray icon, or the menu bar on a Mac. A floating recording button and launch at login can be enabled separately.',
  'highlights.backup.title': 'Move your settings',
  'highlights.backup.desc': 'Export settings, replacements and snippets, then import them on another computer. History, audio and API keys are not included. GitHub also offers a Windows ZIP version that runs without installation.',
